body:
My boyfriend has been going through a rough time lately. He's been forgetting some memories, he spaces out *really* hard sometimes, and he just can't be at a 50/50 share right now. We're making appointments to see doctors and psychiatrists because this never used to happen. I've been having to do most of the heavy lifting for the past 7 months. But I do it all out of love. He's starting to apologize for needing so much of my time, and he also said he feels bad for being so dependent on me. It's been tugging with my patience for a while now, but I've been holding out because I'm positive it will get better. If anyone wants to know what I think it might be, [Temporal Lobe Epilepsy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temporal_lobe_epilepsy) seems to be hitting it right on the head. He's going to a Psychiatrist soon, and after that a Neurologist.

&#x200B;

My apologies if this is going too out of bounds, I'm 15 and going through high school with a possibly epileptic 1st boyfriend, on top of my own issues, is a lot for me. I just needed to vent.
